---
title: Session Management & Revocation
---
%% Listing your active sessions and ending them. Before 2026-08-29 a revoke only stopped the
%% REFRESH token; the access token stayed usable for up to 30 more minutes. It no longer does.
sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    actor U as User
    participant SPA as Angular<br/>SecurityComponent
    participant API as SessionController<br/>/user/sessions
    participant SESS as SessionService
    participant DB as MySQL<br/>refreshsessions
    participant OTHER as Another device<br/>(session B)

    rect rgba(107, 91, 255, 0.10)
    note over U, DB: Review
    U->>SPA: Open the security screen
    SPA->>API: GET /user/sessions
    API->>SESS: listSessions(userId)
    SESS->>DB: Active families for this user
    API-->>SPA: Device, location, last-used per session
    end

    rect rgba(251, 113, 133, 0.12)
    note over U, OTHER: Revoke
    alt end one session
        U->>SPA: "Sign out this device"
        SPA->>API: DELETE /user/sessions/{family}
        API->>SESS: revokeSession(userId, family)
        SESS->>DB: UPDATE ... SET revoked = TRUE WHERE family = :family
    else end every other session
        U->>SPA: "Sign out everywhere else"
        SPA->>API: DELETE /user/sessions
        API->>SESS: revokeOtherSessions(userId, currentFamily)
        SESS->>DB: UPDATE ... SET revoked = TRUE<br/>WHERE user = :id AND family <> :current
        note right of SESS: The caller's own session must survive —<br/>"everywhere else" that also logs you out<br/>is a different, broken feature.
    else password changed
        SESS->>DB: revokeAllSessions(userId) — including this one
    end
    end

    rect rgba(52, 211, 153, 0.10)
    note over OTHER, DB: The effect, on the very next request
    OTHER->>API: Any call with its still-unexpired access token
    API->>DB: TokenProvider → SessionRepo.isFamilyRevoked(sid)
    DB-->>API: revoked = TRUE
    API-->>OTHER: 401 — immediately, not in 30 minutes
    note right of API: One check point closes the gap for ALL<br/>four revoke paths at once, because every<br/>one of them already set the same column.
    end

    note over U, OTHER: Chosen over a per-user token_version counter, which can only revoke<br/>everything at once — wrong for both single-session revoke and<br/>"sign out everywhere else".
